From: kevin <contact@qazsskevin.org>
Subject: [PATCH] xwm: send a synthetic ConfigureNotify for no-op ConfigureRequests

ICCCM 4.1.5: when the window manager handles a ConfigureRequest without
moving or resizing the window, the X server generates no ConfigureNotify,
so the WM has to send a synthetic one.  gamescope only forwarded the
request with XConfigureWindow.

Wine waits for the ConfigureNotify that answers its own configure request
(by serial) and holds every later _NET_WM_STATE, _MOTIF_WM_HINTS and
configure request until it arrives ("is updating config, delaying
request").  MapleStory in windowed 1920x1080 starts with a 1366x768 login
popup and grows it to 1920x1080; gamescope has already stretched the
window to the root by then, so Wine's request for (0,0)-(1920,1080) is a
no-op and never gets an answer.  When the game later switches to a
resizable 1032x802 window for the auction house, nothing reaches the X
server: the 1024x768 client stays in the top-left corner of a 1920x1080
X window.

Compare the request with the current geometry and, when it changes
nothing, send the synthetic event after forwarding the request.

Tested (headless gamescope 1920x1080, probe doing the game's sequence:
1366x768 popup -> 1920x1080 popup -> style 0x14ce0000 at 1032x802 ->
back to the 1920x1080 popup, D3D9 windowed): before, the X window stays
1920x1080 and the picture sits in the top-left corner; after, the X
window is 1024x768 and gamescope scales it to 1440x1080 centred, then
back to 1920x1080.  Needs gamescope-0002 (Wine waits for _NET_WM_STATE
first).

--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -6257,7 +6257,40 @@
 		wlserver_unlock();
 	}
 
+	// ICCCM 4.1.5: a request that does not move or resize the window produces no real
+	// ConfigureNotify, so the window manager has to send a synthetic one.  Wine holds every
+	// later state, hints and configure request until it sees the event for its own request,
+	// so without it a window that once asked for its current geometry never changes again
+	// (MapleStory's auction house stays a 1024x768 client in a 1920x1080 X window).
+	XWindowAttributes attr;
+	bool bSynthetic = XGetWindowAttributes( ctx->dpy, configureRequest->window, &attr ) &&
+		( !( configureRequest->value_mask & CWX ) || changes.x == attr.x ) &&
+		( !( configureRequest->value_mask & CWY ) || changes.y == attr.y ) &&
+		( !( configureRequest->value_mask & CWWidth ) || changes.width == attr.width ) &&
+		( !( configureRequest->value_mask & CWHeight ) || changes.height == attr.height ) &&
+		( !( configureRequest->value_mask & CWBorderWidth ) || changes.border_width == attr.border_width );
+
 	XConfigureWindow( ctx->dpy, configureRequest->window, configureRequest->value_mask, &changes );
+
+	if ( bSynthetic )
+	{
+		XConfigureEvent notify =
+		{
+			.type = ConfigureNotify,
+			.send_event = True,
+			.display = ctx->dpy,
+			.event = configureRequest->window,
+			.window = configureRequest->window,
+			.x = attr.x,
+			.y = attr.y,
+			.width = attr.width,
+			.height = attr.height,
+			.border_width = attr.border_width,
+			.above = None,
+			.override_redirect = attr.override_redirect,
+		};
+		XSendEvent( ctx->dpy, configureRequest->window, False, StructureNotifyMask, (XEvent *)&notify );
+	}
 }
 
 static void circulate_request( xwayland_ctx_t *ctx, XCirculateRequestEvent *circulateRequest )
